// E0320: a name that is not in the shape of its kind (spec 2.3). Each shape is a core that starts with
// a letter, and at most one `_` at the end. A `snake_case` core is lowercase letters, digits and `_`,
// an `UpperCamel` core is letters and digits, an `UPPER_SNAKE` core is capitals, digits and `_`. Two
// `_` in a row (`__`) are never fine, at the end either (`a__`). Each declaration holds one name, and
// the mark is on its line. Names that are fine are in types/naming_shapes_fine.

pub fn a__() -> I32 { //~ E0320
  1
}

